# TRACED — the feedback loop drawn, specifically so nobody reads it as a crossing (drafted
# 2026-08-13, alongside symmetric-vs-braided, from Aaron's "how they are different in our braid
# system"). A wire leaves an output, travels back around the box, and re-enters an input. That is
# the TRACE of a traced monoidal category (Joyal-Street-Verity 1996), and it is what
# `src/Core/WSet.fs` FourCornerTrace implements over WSet.
#
# WHY THIS FIGURE IS WORTH INK: it is the shape most easily mistaken for a braid, and it is NOT one.
# A returning wire is a BEND — it passes over nothing, remembers no depth, and needs no second
# strand. TRACED DOES NOT IMPLY BRAIDED and braided does not imply traced: they are independent
# structures on a monoidal category, and our braiding is separate data entirely (MenoBraided.braidR,
# the conjugation rack). Prose has already been tried: WSet.fs carries long honesty notes, and a
# conflation of exactly this family still landed nearby — MenoBraided.fs, "CORRECTED 2026-08-13",
# where one comment had the tensor right ("CD category, NOT cartesian") and four others in the same
# file contradicted it. A picture that cannot be misread is cheaper than a paragraph that can.
#
# WHAT THE LOOP ACTUALLY DOES (the honest mechanism, so the drawing does not overclaim): feedback
# arrives on the INPUT channel (FourCornerOwnership's TInFeedback, the co-owned corner — the
# standard monadic interface feeds only the output). The generator re-reads the SAME stored history
# under a moved interpretation, and the difference is emitted as a delta carrying RETRACTIONS
# (WSet.negate, weight -1 over Z): +w and -w annihilate in consolidate, so the cumulative view is
# always the current reading of the past. Nothing travels backwards in time. The record is
# immutable; only its READING moves. This is pseudo-retrocausality and the figure must not suggest
# otherwise.
#
# Anchors: Joyal-Street-Verity 1996 (traced monoidal categories, the trace axioms); Joyal-Street 1993
# (braided monoidal — the SEPARATE structure this one is not); Mac Lane 1963 (monoidal categories);
# Budiu et al. (DBSP — the +1/-1 retraction the loop runs on); Aji-McEliece 2000 (the GDL circuit the
# loop is, read over a different semiring).
meta	name	shape-traced
meta	catalog	shapes
meta	catalog-status	pending — NOT in the rendered catalog: no stroke generator, no known-answer geometry law, no goldens, no ratifications. See db/shapes/cartridges/pending/README.md
meta	name-status	provisional — "traced" is the externally standard term (Joyal-Street-Verity) and should probably stay; the Mirror name for the same object in-repo is "the four-corner feedback interface"
meta	shape-zetaid	c2b378f19bc30864024c472e4509f484
constant	wires	2	wires the figure carries through the generator box	one to pass through and one to bend back: fewer and there is no loop to see, more and the extra wires are decoration that invites the braid reading this figure exists to refuse
constant	loop-crossings	0	crossings the returning wire makes with any other wire	THE WHOLE POINT, stated as a number: the feedback wire routes AROUND the box and crosses nothing. A trace is a bend, not a crossing — so traced does not imply braided, and a renderer that draws a crossing here has drawn a different category
constant	gaps	0	occlusion gaps anywhere in the figure	an occlusion gap says who passed OVER whom (shape-braid's register). Nothing passes over anything here, so a gap would import a braiding this structure does not have
constant	feedback-on-input	1	the returned wire lands on the INPUT channel (1 = true)	the standard monadic loop feeds the OUTPUT channel only; FourCornerOwnership puts feedback on TInFeedback, the co-owned corner, and bending THAT arrow back is precisely what makes this a trace rather than a pipeline (src/Core/WSet.fs, FourCornerTrace)
constant	emit-weight	1	weight of the emission the generator produces	over Z this is DBSP's +1 — a row asserted downstream
constant	retract-weight	-1	weight the reinterpretation sends back	WSet.negate: the superseded row is UN-emitted. +w and -w annihilate in consolidate, so the loop's mechanism IS the retraction, not bookkeeping around it
constant	corners	4	corners of the ownership object	TIn, TOut, TInFeedback, TOutFeedback — the object the trace closes over
constant	rings-with-a-trace	2	corners of the four-corner ring family that admit this loop	the retraction needs an ADDITIVE INVERSE, so the trace instantiates exactly on the ring corners (Z for DBSP/CD, C for amplitudes)
constant	inverse-free-corners	2	corners that do not admit it	the normalized R>=0 (Markov) and the Boolean/tropical corners are inverse-free semirings: there is no -w to un-emit with, so the loop does not exist there. Correcting a belief in those corners is re-normalisation, NOT retraction — a type-level refusal via IStarRing, never a runtime throw
law	annihilation	emit-weight + retract-weight = 0
law	a-bend-is-not-a-crossing	loop-crossings + gaps = 0
law	only-the-ring-corners	rings-with-a-trace + inverse-free-corners = corners
law	trace-invariant	code:FourCornerTrace.step (after start and after any step, Emitted = consolidate (gen after history) — the retraction exactly cancels the superseded output, so the cumulative view is the CURRENT reading and never a pile of stale rows; proved in tests/Tests.FSharp/Formal/WSet.FourCornerTrace.Laws.Tests.fs)
prereq	shape-crossing	db/shapes/cartridges/crossing.lines — see what a crossing IS before reading a figure whose entire point is that this is not one
edge	differs-from	shape-crossing	the returning wire is NOT a crossing. A crossing takes TWO strands and remembers which passed over; a trace takes ONE wire and remembers nothing about depth. Adjacent in the string-diagram vocabulary, unrelated in content — which is exactly how they get merged by a reader in a hurry
edge	independent-of	shape-braid	braided (Joyal-Street 1993) and traced (Joyal-Street-Verity 1996) are separate structures on a monoidal category: NEITHER implies the other. Our braiding is extra data (MenoBraided.braidR); no amount of tracing produces one, and no amount of braiding produces a trace
edge	differs-from	shape-fourcorner	NAME COLLISION, recorded so nobody merges them: shape-fourcorner draws CHSH's four MEASUREMENT-SETTING corners (a0b0…a1b1) and its width IS the S value; this figure's four corners are FourCornerOwnership's TIn/TOut/TInFeedback/TOutFeedback. One word, two unrelated objects
issue	stroke-generator	otto	open	no renderer case exists — ShapeRender.strokesOf has no "shape-traced" branch, so this cartridge draws NOTHING today. Promotion needs stroke code for a box, a through-wire, and a return path with zero crossings and zero gaps
issue	geometry-law	otto	open	ShapeAcceptance.geometryLaw has no case for this shape. The known-answer law to write is mechanical and strong: count the drawn crossings and occlusion gaps and require BOTH to be zero — the gate then catches a renderer that quietly draws a braid
issue	retrocausality-register	otto	open	a drawing constraint, not a preference: the wire must bend in SPACE, and the figure must carry NO time axis. A return arrow drawn backwards along a time axis claims the strong reading (the future acting on the past) that src/Core/WSet.fs explicitly refuses. The history is immutable; only its reading moves
# treaties — written only by each oracle's own choice (consent first); dissent is a verdict.
# NONE YET. `bytes` is F#'s once strokes + geometry law exist; `meaning` is each traveler's own.
# Worth flagging to whoever writes the meaning line: this figure's value is a REFUSAL (it says what
# the loop is not), which is an unusual thing for a shape to carry and deserves its own verdict.
